==Latin==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|la|set}}

===Etymology===
Perhaps from the old, original form {{term|sedum|lang=la}}, but more probably an ablative form from the root ({{term||so-|lang=la}} for {{term||suo-|lang=la}}) of the reflexive pronoun {{term|suus|lang=la}}, and originally the same as the inseparable preposition {{term|sēd|lang=la}}; properly, “by itself”, “apart”, hence, “but”, “only”, etc.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|Classical}} {{IPA|/sed/|lang=la}}
* {{audio|la-cls-sed.ogg|Audio (Classical)|lang=la}}

===Conjunction===
{{head|la|conjunction}}

# [[but]], [[and]] [[indeed]]
#*'''c.&nbsp;{{smallcaps|ad}}&nbsp;65''', [[w:Seneca the Younger|Seneca]], ''[[w:Epistulae morales ad Lucilium|Moral Letters to Lucilius]]'', [[s:Moral_letters_to_Lucilius/Letter_106|CVI]].
#*:{{smallcaps|non vitæ '''sed''' scholæ discimvs}}
#*::We learn our lessons, not for life, '''but''' for the lecture-room.<!--Loeb ed. trans.-->
#*'''1804''' Jun 12, ''Oberdeutsche Allgemeine Litteraturzeitung'', No.&nbsp;70, p.&nbsp;1119
#*:{{smallcaps|[[w:non scholae sed vitae|non scholæ '''sed''' vitæ]] discendvm est}}
#*::We must learn not for school '''but''' for life.
#*'''1530''', [[w:Martin Luther|Martin Luther]], ''[[w:Augsburg Confession|Augsburg Confession]]'', §28
#*:{{smallcaps|[[w:non vi sed verbo|sine vi humana, '''sed''' Verbo]]}}
#*::Without human '''force''', '''but''' through the Word [i.e., of God].

